windows: a line's height leaves out the font's line gap

DirectWriteTextSystem::layout_line took a line's ascent and descent
from DWRITE_LINE_METRICS, whose baseline and height include the font's
line gap. Fonts without USE_TYPO_METRICS whose hhea line gap exceeds
the gap between their win metrics (IBM Plex Sans SC: hhea 0.88/0.12
plus 1.0, win 1.06/0.44) gained half an em, so text centred in a fixed
line height sat low: an overflow-hidden line cut its descenders and
digits fell to the bottom of a pill (Ely R22.1). CoreText and
cosmic-text report ascent and descent without the gap. The layout's
format now disables the gap (IDWriteTextFormat3::SetLineSpacing,
DWRITE_FONT_LINE_GAP_USAGE_DISABLED; Windows 10 1709 and later).

DWRITE_LINE_SPACING: https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/win32/api/dwrite_3/ns-dwrite_3-dwrite_line_spacing

diff --git a/vendor/gpui-pre-windows/src/direct_write.rs b/vendor/gpui-pre-windows/src/direct_write.rs
index bfa50ffc..9ee590aa 100644
--- a/vendor/gpui-pre-windows/src/direct_write.rs
+++ b/vendor/gpui-pre-windows/src/direct_write.rs
@@ -530,6 +530,13 @@ impl DirectWriteState {
                 if let Some(ref fallbacks) = font_info.fallbacks {
                     format.SetFontFallback(fallbacks)?;
                 }
+                // No line gap, as on macOS and Linux.
+                let spacing: IDWriteTextFormat3 = format.cast()?;
+                spacing.SetLineSpacing(&DWRITE_LINE_SPACING {
+                    method: DWRITE_LINE_SPACING_METHOD_DEFAULT,
+                    fontLineGapUsage: DWRITE_FONT_LINE_GAP_USAGE_DISABLED,
+                    ..Default::default()
+                })?;
 
                 let layout = components.factory.CreateTextLayout(
                     text_wide,
